{"title":"2004 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Lloyd is practising his arithmetic by taking the reciprocal of a number and by adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to a number.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(add images to problem 1 page)\n</p><p>Taking the reciprocal of a number is denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Here is an example of Lloyd’s work, starting with an input of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the five steps from (b), what input should you begin with to get a final result of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72daad28fe802075b00bd15eaf0789788b6902a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{14}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />? Justify your answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the solution to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b\" title=\"2004 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1b\">part b</a>, the final result was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/7/ad766846893772338455f423b07d12d28e95a09a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1 + x}{1 + 2x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"57\" height=\"40\" />. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/0/e207bfdf250e225785c12a30af4781ab159e3451.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1 + x}{1 + 2x} = \\frac{14}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"103\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271656070958eb24e7a1eae9f6dc90e91cf3407d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27(1 + x) = 14(1 + 2x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/f/cbfe1e3ab19e1033e44c9ce6851f9191bfd63a79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27 + 27x = 14 + 28x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"164\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54bd0055839aff8efe1399ab05a71bdc9587ef77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28x - 27x = 27 - 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"164\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/1/8a1e6256137540c4e292dbe4ffc0ba6f7d597eb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x = 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"66\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>Alternatively, we could have noticed by inspection of the initial fraction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/1/8a1e6256137540c4e292dbe4ffc0ba6f7d597eb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x = 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"66\" height=\"25\" /> would work.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017203744\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.024 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 59/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1756/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2379/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.359      1 2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%   13.359      1 -total\n 40.14%    5.362      2 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36916:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017203744 and revision id 285708. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}